{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:23:56.026Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `project_git_root` and `NestedRoot` in the vcs kernel:\n\n- **`crates/kernel/vcs/src/project_root.rs`** — new module holding the `NestedRoot` error with public `root`/`top` fields, the exact TypeScript message, a `std::error::Error` impl, and `project_git_root(root, config)`. It skips git when `vcs.enabled` is false, reads the top level via `GitVcs::new(root).with_timeouts(...).root()`, canonicalizes the root, and compares both paths in a pure helper.\n- **`crates/kernel/vcs/src/lib.rs`** — declares and re-exports both items.\n- **`crates/kernel/vcs/tests/project_root.rs`** — covers every row of the \"Project root check outcomes\" table plus the error trait/public-field requirements.\n\nVerification:\n- `cargo test -p osq-kernel-vcs --test project_root` — passes\n- `cargo mutants -p osq-kernel-vcs -f crates/kernel/vcs/src/project_root.rs` — 10/10 caught\n- Proposal verify (`pnpm verify` + `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh`) with `OSQ_CHANGE` — passes\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/315-vcs-root-fails-fast/.run/results/2.md`."}}
